    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0135" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg125"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Private.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Ross to Mr.
                        Jackson.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> I send with this a letter to you with
                    reference to the memorial to the President. You can prepare your letter to Mr.
                    Seward, so as to have it ready for forwarding with the memorial per steamer.</p>
                <p>The names given in the accompanying letter represent a large amount of wealth as
                    well as respectability. Indeed, no community could furnish eight names more
                    universally or deservedly respected.</p>
                <pb facs="0136" n="126" xml:id="pg126"/>
                <p>The memorial will be sent up to your office this afternoon. I send a printed copy
                    in the letter to you, which you should, I think, forward to Mr. Seward, along
                    with the memorial. I send also a printed copy for your own use. In the event of
                    the President making a reply, which no doubt he will, the acknowledgment of the
                    memorial, if made to the <hi rendition="#italic">gentlemen whose names are
                        mentioned</hi> in the letter to you, would be better than if made to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">one individual;</hi> but all that will be arranged by
                    Hon. Mr. Seward and yourself.</p>
                <p>Yours, sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>DONALD ROSS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">M. M. Jackson,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
